        "note": {
          "en": "Each cell is shaded by \\(f=x+y\\) at its midpoint over \\([0,2]^2\\). Refine the grid and the midpoint sum converges to \\(8\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "heading": "Double integrals in polar coordinates",
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>For circular regions, polar coordinates simplify everything — but the area element gains a factor of \\( r \\):</p>\\[ \\iint_{R} f\\,dA=\\iint f(r\\cos\\theta,\\,r\\sin\\theta)\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta. \\]<p>That extra \\( r \\) is the Jacobian of the polar change of variables, and forgetting it is the most common error in the topic.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Double integral",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\iint_R f\\,dA \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Iterated",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\int\\!\\!\\int f\\,dy\\,dx \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\iint_R dA \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Polar",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( r\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 14.A — An iterated integral",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\!\\!\\int_0^2 (x+2y)\\,dx\\,dy \\).</p><p>Integrate in \\( x \\) first, treating \\( y \\) as constant:</p>\\[ \\int_0^1\\Big[\\tfrac{x^{2}}{2}+2xy\\Big]_0^2 dy=\\int_0^1(2+4y)\\,dy=\\big[2y+2y^{2}\\big]_0^1=4. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 14.B — Area of a disk in polar",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Confirm the area of the unit disk \\( x^{2}+y^{2}\\le 1 \\) using a polar double integral.</p>\\[ \\iint_{R} dA=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\!\\!\\int_0^1 r\\,dr\\,d\\theta=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\tfrac12\\,d\\theta=\\pi. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
